Time Complexity:

Let n be the input

    Each call makes 2 recursive calls:
    T(n) = T(n-1) + T(n-2)

Overall: O(2^n)


Space Complexity:

    Recursion stack depth = n

Overall: O(n)


Approach:

1. Handle base cases:
   - If n == 0 → return 0
   - If n == 1 → return 1

2. For other cases:
   - Recursively compute:
     → fib(n-1)
     → fib(n-2)

3. Return sum of both results

4. This builds recursion tree and computes answer






class Solution {
    public int nthFibonacci(int n) {
       if(n==0 || n==1) return n;
       return nthFibonacci(n-1) + nthFibonacci(n-2);
    }
}
